      "side": 1,
      "message": "Agree with Junyu on the check referenced by the link. Really, you can simplify this code to this:\n\n    final NetworkRequest req \u003d nri.isMultilayerRequest() ? \n        nri.getActiveRequest() : nri.mRequests.get(0);\n        \nAdditionally you should update the comment to:\n\n    // Non-multilayer listen requests do not have an active request.\n    \nA multilayer requests will have something for nri.getActiveRequest() on CALLBACK_AVAILABLE whether it is a listen or request type. The only case it won\u0027t have one is for a non-multilayer listen which you did a good job of catching.\n\nAs for the log:\n\n    log.wtf if nri.getActiveRequest() \u003d\u003d null\n    \nI\u0027ll defer to you on the log, but the check would be:\n\n    if (nri.isMultilayerRequest() \u0026\u0026 nri.getActiveRequest() \u003d\u003d null) log.wtf",
